2. Frontend specification
2.1 Design system
• Tokens: CSS variables for color, spacing (4 px scale), radius, elevation, type scale. Light and dark themes. A brand palette with one primary, one accent, and semantic success/warning/danger/info colors. Minimum contrast WCAG 2.2 AA.
• Typography: Inter for Latin, Noto Sans Devanagari for Nepali, loaded with font-display: swap and subset to reduce weight. Line height tuned for Devanagari (1.6+).
• Components (build and document in Storybook): Button, IconButton, Input, PhoneInput (+977), OTPInput, Select, Combobox (skills, locations), MultiSelect, DateRangePicker, Slider (salary), Tabs, Dialog, Drawer, BottomSheet, Toast, Skeleton, EmptyState, Badge (verification levels), Avatar, DataTable (virtualized), KanbanBoard, Stepper, FileDropzone, ProgressRing, Chart wrappers, Stat card, Timeline, RichTextEditor (job descriptions).
• Trust components: VerificationBadge (self-reported / document submitted / identity checked / education checked / employer confirmed / assessment completed) with a popover stating exactly what was checked, by whom and when. ExplainabilityPanel showing why a job or candidate was matched. SponsorDisclosure bar on every rewards task.
2.2 Information architecture and routing
Use route groups so one codebase serves four experiences with role-aware layouts.
(app)/            Job seeker shell, bottom nav: Home, Jobs, Gigs, Rewards, Profile
(employer)/       Employer shell: Dashboard, Post Job, Applicants, Talent, Company
(sponsor)/        Sponsor campaign dashboard
(admin)/          Admin console (desktop-first, sidebar)
(public)/         SEO pages: /jobs, /jobs/[slug], /companies/[slug], /salaries, /learn
(auth)/           Sign in, sign up, OTP, role switch, recovery
A role switcher in the profile menu changes active role and organization context. The active context is stored server-side in the session and echoed into every request; the UI never trusts its own copy.
2.3 State, data and offline
• Server state in TanStack Query with typed query keys per domain. Optimistic updates only for non-financial actions (save job, follow, mark notification read).
• Client UI state in Zustand, small and local. No financial or permission state stored client-side.
• PWA with a service worker (Workbox): app-shell precache, stale-while-revalidate for job lists, background sync for drafts and application submissions, offline banner and queued-action indicators.
• Resumable uploads (tus) for CVs and sponsor videos; client-side image compression before upload; images served as AVIF/WebP with responsive sizes.
• Realtime subscriptions (Supabase Realtime) only for messages, application status, notifications and wallet confirmations.
