3. Database specification
3.1 Conventions
• PostgreSQL 15+, extensions: pgcrypto, pg_trgm, unaccent, vector, pg_cron, postgis, btree_gin.
• Primary keys uuid (gen_random_uuid()); timestamps timestamptz; soft delete via deleted_at; money as bigint minor units (paisa) plus currency char(3).
• Every table has created_at, updated_at; tenant tables carry organization_id. Enums as Postgres enum types or lookup tables.
• Schemas: core, jobs, recruit, gigs, network, rewards, hr, ops, ai. Public access only through views and RPCs.
• Row-Level Security enabled on every table, default deny. Policy helper functions: auth.uid(), core.has_role(role), core.is_org_member(org_id, min_role).
