6. Build sequence (give the AI builder one step at a time)
1.  Foundation: monorepo, design system, i18n, auth with phone OTP, roles, organizations, RLS test harness, CI.
2.  Marketplace core: candidate profiles, employer verification, job posting, hybrid search, apply, application tracking, CV storage, admin verification queue.
3.  Professional recruitment: ATS Kanban, questionnaires, rosters, branding pages, scheduling, analytics, subscriptions.
4.  AI layer: AI gateway, resume parse and studio, match engine with explanations, JD generator, interview coach, voice search, scam scoring, Auto Apply.
5.  Ecosystem: Skill Passport and assessments, Gigs, Network, local worker marketplace, Insta Hire, HR workspace.
6.  Rewards (gated): only after signed sponsor agreements, funded budgets, payout partner and legal review. Build ledger, task sessions, risk engine, manual payouts first.
7.  Global: multi-currency, country rules, regional languages, country-specific verification.
After each step, the builder must output: migrations applied, RLS tests passing, new env vars, open risks, and the next step's prerequisites.
7. Product rules carried over from the PRD
• Rewards are optional, sponsor-funded, and never described as guaranteed income or employment; no payment for clicking ads.
• Basic job search and applying stay free; payment never guarantees a job or interview.
• Verification labels state exactly what was checked.
• Recruiter discovery is opt-in, contact details are hidden until the candidate authorises access.
• Gig payments use a legally reviewed payment partner; the platform does not hold customer funds as an unlicensed escro